some suggestions to make nethack3.0 more accessible:

dlev1 should be void of all traps, sinks, fountains altars.
dlev1 should be void of doors and chests.
dlev1 should create orcs without knives until a player attains lev3
  experience or leaves the level and returns (ditto for h's).
oracles should appear between dlevs 3 and 5 with lower prices:
  $25 for rumors, $250 for consultations.
a few more topics for the oracles wouldn't hurt (don't give away the farm):
  advice on kicking things,
  advice on elbereth,
  advice on prayer and sacrifice,
  advice on pet behavior,
  advice on intrinsic attributes (i.e.)
    of all the travelers in the dungeon only archeologists can recognize
gems at first glance. however there are intrinsic attributes that you
may possess including resistance to fire, cold, magic, and sleep. consuming
quivering blob meat can make you feel healthy thus providing resistance
to poison. there are other resistances, and you may become fast, invisible
and telepathic. teleportation and teleport control are also highly prized,
along with other untold intrinsics.

shopkeepers should be able to give oracles (randomly in response to chat)
  but at twice the price ($50 for rumors, $500 for consultations).
shopkeepers should be able to randomly provide insight into items that
  they are knowledgable of (i.e. shop type) at a price of $500.
magic traps should include the possibility of providing insight,
  enlightenment and free consultations.
tyros should somehow be steered towards playing priest characters to
  get them familiar with the all-important blessed/cursed modes of items.
explore-mode goes unused because it doesn't get your name up there in
  lights, so perhaps explore-mode games could post scores with a clearly
  labelled flag designating that progress as such. whether to post the
  score or not should require confirmation. you should not be able to get
  consultations in explore-mode.
****************
i think the above changes can lower the high-threshold against early
survival and also disseminate more useful/necessary information to all
players, two areas that nethack3.0 could use some help in. this should
ease the frustration felt by many players who die before they really
enter the dungeon. nethack3.0 is intrinsically hard but the above
changes should make it more approachable.

